# Drafted by Gemini (R14 aftermath), edited.

~ courtyard
Narrator: Cold wind sweeps the flagstones, carrying the sour ash of old pyres. The Crimson Faithful gather in their red wool, silent and staring at the cathedral doors.
faithful_novice [afraid]: The bells have stopped. Where is the Abbot? Who tends the garden now?
* [if flag.renathyr_journal] Hold up the journal as proof. -> reveal
* Tell them what the Rose really is. -> reveal_plain
* Say nothing. -> hush

~ reveal
cutscene mon_reveal
cutscene mon_reveal_2
Narrator: You read Father Marius's own hand to the crowd, every dry word of his bargain and his shame. One by one, red hoods are pulled down into the snow.
faithful_scribe [sad]: It was his own hand. I know his ink. We burned our neighbors for a fiend's supper.
set crimson_rose_revealed
set crimson_faith_disbanded
-> successor

~ reveal_plain
Narrator: Your voice rings off the red glass, naming the devil beneath the altar. Half the courtyard shrinks back in horror; the rest only clutch their thorns tighter.
faithful_novice [angry]: You lie! The Rose bled for us, and you murdered her shepherd in the dark!
faithful_cook [weary]: Hush, boy. Smell the cellar air coming up those stairs. That was never a goddess.
set crimson_rose_revealed
-> successor

~ hush
Narrator: You offer them neither sermon nor excuse. The red-robed folk stand in the drifting snow like sheep whose penned gate has blown open in the night.
faithful_novice [weary]: No word at all? Not even a prayer for the ash?
-> successor

~ successor
set crimson_successor = "none"
if not flag.mon_jaeger_done
set crimson_successor = "jaeger"
endif
if not flag.mon_cromwell_done
set crimson_successor = "cromwell"
endif
if not flag.mon_olaf_done
set crimson_successor = "olaf"
endif
Narrator: An empty chair in a high house never stays cold for long; whatever remains of the abbey's masters will soon enough decide what becomes of the flock.
quest the_priors settled
set crimson_aftermath
if not quest.crimson_monastery >= aftermath
quest crimson_monastery aftermath
endif
-> END

~ farewell
cutscene mon_moon_white
cutscene mon_moon_white_2
if not quest.crimson_monastery >= return
quest crimson_monastery return
endif
set crimson_farewell
set act2_done += 1
# Act II raises the party four levels, 4 to 8, whichever chapters they are (plan 5.1): the fifth chapter done gives none.
if flag.act2_done <= 4
xp milestone
endif
Narrator: Down in Dawn's Gate, the red stain washes from the clouds, leaving the old crone's moon bone-white above the pines. The smell of wet silver and woodsmoke returns to the lane.
kristoff_gruber [neutral]: Ale's on the board, and the shutters are unbarred. You best get down the river road before I start charging you rent.
dg_halka_wren [weary]: The bells are quiet up the hill. That will do for tonight. Safe road to you, strangers.
-> END
